<h2><%= type.model_name.human %>s</h2>

<% if type.model_name == LowIncomeCode.to_s %>
  <p>These codes are for only those who have made low income applications and have been approved.</p>
<% elsif type.model_name == MembershipCode.to_s %>
  <p>
    These codes are automatically assigned to every user in the system and allow for general sale tickets.
    Typically, you will not need to generate these codes as they get automatically generated.
  </p>
<% elsif type.model_name == DirectSaleCode.to_s %>
  <p>These codes are only for those who need a direct sale as they either missed the general sale or another situation.</p>
<% else %>
  <p>Unknown code type '<%= type.model_name %>', please contact an admin to alert them to this issue.</p>
<% end %>

<h3>Generate</h3>
<%= bootstrap_form_tag url: admin_codes_path, id: type.model_name.human.downcase.gsub!(' ', '-') do |f| %>
  <%= f.number_field :number,
                     hide_label: true,
                     placeholder: 'Number of codes to generate',
                     id: "#{type.model_name.human.downcase.gsub!(' ', '-')}-number",
                     append: f.primary('Generate'),
                     input_group_class: 'input-group-lg' %>
  <%= f.hidden_field :type, :value => type %>
<% end %>

<h3>Status</h3>
<p><%= t('assigned_codes', count: type.taken.count) %>. <%= t('codes', count: type.available.count) %></p>
<p>
  Use this list to import into Eventbrite <%= link_to "Download codes CSV", admin_codes_path(format: :csv, type: type) %>
</p>
